  "clinical_evidence": [
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_001",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Mixed, I suppose. Better than last year. But I've been avoiding team meetings again, and I keep worrying that means I'm sliding backwards. Is that what it means?",
      "start_timestamp": "00:45",
      "end_timestamp": "01:00",
      "supports": [
        "chief_complaint",
        "symptoms[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Three months, roughly. Since we got a new manager who likes everyone to speak up. I just find a reason to be somewhere else.",
      "start_timestamp": "01:14",
      "end_timestamp": "01:27",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "It's very human, and it's good that you can see the pattern. What about the panic attacks you had last year? Where are those now?",
      "start_timestamp": "01:59",
      "end_timestamp": "02:11",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Oh, those have gone. Honestly gone, I haven't had one since the summer. I keep expecting one to come back, though.",
      "start_timestamp": "02:13",
      "end_timestamp": "02:25",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Sertraline, 100 milligrams once a day, in the morning. And the omeprazole, 20 milligrams, also every morning. Then propranolol, 10 milligrams, only when I've got a presentation.",
      "start_timestamp": "02:42",
      "end_timestamp": "02:54",
      "supports": [
        "medications[0]",
        "medications[1]",
        "medications[2]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Many people stay on sertraline for a good while, and it's doing a job for you. I've got in your notes social anxiety, reflux and eczema. Is that all still accurate?",
      "start_timestamp": "03:26",
      "end_timestamp": "03:40",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.past_medical_history[0]",
        "medical_history.past_medical_history[1]",
        "medical_history.past_medical_history[2]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Yes, that's all of it. Though the eczema is mostly quiet now, just my hands in winter.",
      "start_timestamp": "03:42",
      "end_timestamp": "03:52",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.past_medical_history[0]",
        "medical_history.past_medical_history[1]",
        "medical_history.past_medical_history[2]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Only my tonsils, when I was nine. I don't remember much, just the ice cream afterwards.",
      "start_timestamp": "04:01",
      "end_timestamp": "04:10",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.surgical_history[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "That's the best part, of course. Now I need to ask about some darker thoughts, which I ask everybody. Any thoughts of harming yourself?",
      "start_timestamp": "04:13",
      "end_timestamp": "04:26",
      "supports": [
        "negative_findings[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "No, no. Never like that. It's more that I feel stupid and ashamed, not that I want to... no.",
      "start_timestamp": "04:28",
      "end_timestamp": "04:38",
      "supports": [
        "negative_findings[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "I'm glad you told me, and feeling ashamed is something we can work on together. And when your heart does race, any chest pain or fainting?",
      "start_timestamp": "04:40",
      "end_timestamp": "04:56",
      "supports": [
        "negative_findings[1]",
        "negative_findings[2]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "No, no chest pain and no fainting. It's only that nervous thumping, and then it passes. Is that normal?",
      "start_timestamp": "04:58",
      "end_timestamp": "05:07",
      "supports": [
        "negative_findings[1]",
        "negative_findings[2]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "It's a common pattern, and it's reassuring that there's no pain. Now a few quick questions about the rest of your body. Any problems with your breathing?",
      "start_timestamp": "05:10",
      "end_timestamp": "05:23",
      "supports": [
        "review_of_systems[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "No, my breathing's fine. I even jogged up the stairs this morning because I was worried about being late.",
      "start_timestamp": "05:25",
      "end_timestamp": "05:35",
      "supports": [
        "review_of_systems[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Okay. And your stomach and digestion on the omeprazole, any trouble there?",
      "start_timestamp": "05:38",
      "end_timestamp": "05:43",
      "supports": [
        "review_of_systems[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "No, that's all settled, thankfully. Nothing at all.",
      "start_timestamp": "05:46",
      "end_timestamp": "05:50",
      "supports": [
        "review_of_systems[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Good. Do you have any allergies to medicines or anything else?",
      "start_timestamp": "05:53",
      "end_timestamp": "05:58",
      "supports": [
        "negative_findings[3]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "No, none that I know of. I was always asked this at the dentist and never had anything.",
      "start_timestamp": "05:59",
      "end_timestamp": "06:09",
      "supports": [
        "negative_findings[3]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Great. Let me take your measurements now. Blood pressure is 124 over 78.",
      "start_timestamp": "06:18",
      "end_timestamp": "06:25",
      "supports": [
        "vital_signs[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Pulse is 84 and regular. Temperature is 36.5 degrees. Oxygen saturation is 99 percent.",
      "start_timestamp": "06:27",
      "end_timestamp": "06:35",
      "supports": [
        "vital_signs[1]",
        "vital_signs[2]",
        "vital_signs[3]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "84 is perfectly normal, even a little relaxed. Your weight is 78 kilograms, and your breathing rate is 14 a minute.",
      "start_timestamp": "06:48",
      "end_timestamp": "06:59",
      "supports": [
        "vital_signs[4]",
        "vital_signs[5]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Hold your hands out for me, fingers spread. Your hands are steady, there's no tremor, and no sweating on the palms.",
      "start_timestamp": "07:11",
      "end_timestamp": "07:22",
      "supports": [
        "physical_examination[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "They're not. Now, I'd like to arrange a blood test, to check your thyroid and blood count. Anxiety can sometimes be mimicked or worsened by those.",
      "start_timestamp": "07:30",
      "end_timestamp": "07:43",
      "supports": [
        "procedures_and_investigations[0]",
        "clinical_actions[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "No, I don't think that, it's simply a sensible thing to check at a review. I'd also like to book an ECG, since you take propranolol.",
      "start_timestamp": "07:54",
      "end_timestamp": "08:06",
      "supports": [
        "procedures_and_investigations[1]",
        "clinical_actions[1]"
      ]
    }
